	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="14"><b>Headline: Mini-Raid in Lower Guk... thousands die...</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=22">Leafblighter</a> - On July 10, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">Several members of Drakkon's participated in a small raid in Lower Guk.  <br>The primary target was the Ghoul Assassin, who spawns rarely in the <br>Ass/sup room.<br><br>Although things got off to a slow and tragic start trying to actually *get*<br>to the spawn point, once we finally made it, there were no deaths for a<br>good 3-4 (maybe even 5) hours.  Mikuras was able to loot her Mask of <br>Deception (the primary purpose of the raid), and although Vincentt didn't<br>get his.... he still made out like a bandit by winning a new breastplate, <br>shoulderpads, and a weight reduction bag (65%!).<br><br>We suffered only one group wipe-out, due to a bad pull and room <br>respawns.  Ironically, the Ghoul Assassin was one of the mobs that <br>spawned in the room... he was killed, but his body rotted before we were<br>able to get Vincentt a rez so he could loot it.  <br><br>All in all it was quite a successful event.  During most of it, we <br>controlled and cleared not only the Assup room, but also the Savant<br>and Cavalier rooms... all the way down to the Safe Hall.  For those of <br>you unfamiliar with Lower Guk, this is basically half of the entire dead <br>side... no normal group would've been able to do this successfully for<br>any length of time.<br><br>The only other death was suffered by Mikuras.  She and I were screwing <br>around by dueling hand to hand.  I kinda sorta used Instill Doubt on her,<br>it unexpectedly hit, and she was feared for a good 20 seconds or so...<br>just long enough for her to run into some unfriendly MOBs and get the<br>snot beaten out of her.  She received a 90% rez, so I only feel 10% as<br>bad as I did when it happened, but that's still a lot!<br><br>Guild Participants: Amoret, Ranian, Mikuras, Vincentt, Broopus (extra <br>thanks to our level 58 magician and his pet), and myself.  Dartanas<br>popped up near the end to say hi and help us kill a few, but then we<br>disbanded... as Vincentt needed to leave and since we were camping the<br>mask for him, no reason to stay around =)<br><br></td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="13"><b>Drakkon and Evening event.</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=27">Orion</a> - On July 7, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">The other night, I was talking to people in our guild and an enchanter friend of mine from Evening Reign about maybe finishing off the pre epic quest for enchanters. What this entailed was the killing of a lvl 55 rogue triggered spawn in West Karana. I thought in the end we would only get maybe a dozen or so people together. In the end we had about 3 groups of people from both of our guilds and mounted a very successful dual guild effort in taking him down twice. <br><br>I think this was a very successful venture, and hope that we will do more together with all my friends from Evening Reign. <br><br>Bosenberry and I would like to send thank off to <br>Treowe, Sdadar Clatene, Obino, Kinolin, and Thundore(;)) from Drakkon's <br>and <br>Arianche, Tanandas, Grennath, Defoor, Corosa, Hollito, Belt(=)) and Erruen from Bosen's guild, Evening Reign and of course Hluast for her help as well =).<br><br>Thanks to anyone I missed, as well as to the people who hoped to make it but for what ever reason couldn't make it. Bosenberry and I both appreciate it.</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="12"><b>Summary of trip to Kedge Keep.</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=27">Orion</a> - On June 11, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">After much uncertainty, and some hesitation 6 of us over 40 were able to get together for a little outing.<br><br>Clatene, Obino, Sdadar, Speechlessag, Trowsk and myself(as Abyena) were finally able to work everything out and get together for a rather successful trip deep into Kedge keep.<br><br>We started out by heading down and cleared out of the minor spawns, to let everyone get their bearings, and then continued to slay sharks, and kick some mermaid tail! In the end we ended not only clearing bubble's den, but all the mobs in the area and cleared Esterella's temple!<br><br>Unfortunatly, after this it was getting late, and Speechlessag had to go to get some rest, with everyone else getting a tad weary as well. So we decided to give one rare a try and headed off to smite the shark, Cauldronboil, we were doing quite well! But, as luck would have it, we were forced to give up when he was down to a mere fraction of his health with a vow that we will return soon, and finish what we started!<br><br>All in all, a great job by all! Its not easy getting used to fighting underwater! I had lots of fun, and i do believe that everyone else did as well.<br>Let Kedge be warned! We WILL be back!</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="11"><b>Zone Guide launched</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=23">Matrim</a> - On June 7, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">I have added a VERY useful tool to the site.<br><br>The <a href="hunting.asp">Zone Guide</a> will let you know what to do in zones and what zones you should be at for your level.<br><br>Only members can add to it but all can benefit. I will make a link for it in the menu when I redesign it.</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="10"><b>RE:Dark Elf Corruptor goes down 5 times.</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=24">Nolil</a> - On May 29, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">The guild had 5 members that needed the drop for their druid/ranger epic from the DE Corruptor in east karana. He went down 5 times in a tad over 7 hours on  memorial day weekend, Sunday. In addition, the two dark reavers that spawn were killed everytime. Two of the spawns, triggered, no deaths were involved the other three times, approx. 5 people died altogeter.<br>There were many members present at this event. Thanks to all of you. This is another sign of the growth of this guild. Very Good job guild. Keep on keeping on.<br><br>In addition, Tarbul is now a piece of cake. He went down several times. Aaldaar looted the drop for his epic quest.<br>Nolil</td>
	</tr>
	
